        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07084788732394365,
        "y0": 0.7475958286744828,
        "x1": 0.35828383887323934,
        "y1": 0.7539771166079205
      },
      "text": "Bot wlatesome glete and lopird blode",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2510039436619718,
        "y0": 0.7589481773131034,
        "x1": 0.4623363091830985,
        "y1": 0.7660064003450162
      },
      "text": "MS. Lincoln A. i. 17, f. 270.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07044304225352112,
        "y0": 0.7719584848275862,
        "x1": 0.2392634366197183,
        "y1": 0.779840059853019
      },
      "text": "Thare dwelled a man in a myrke donjowne.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07003819718309857,
        "y0": 0.7843329106358621,
        "x1": 0.37568408000000025,
        "y1": 0.7918731671440666
      },
      "text": "And in a fowlestede of corrupcyowne,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07003819718309857,
        "y0": 0.7962729353103449,
        "x1": 0.2538419076056337,
        "y1": 0.8037557654477276
      },
      "text": "Whare he had no fode,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07084788732394365,
        "y0": 0.8088173471875861,
        "x1": 0.3724509872676056,
        "y1": 0.8155131865466017
      },
      "text": "Bot wlatsome glette and lopyrd blode.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.24817002816901407,
        "y0": 0.8213073585668966,
        "x1": 0.4623346898028167,
        "y1": 0.8282729458371207
      },
      "text": "Hampole, MS. Bowes, p. 25.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.030768225352112672,
        "y0": 0.83252121564,
        "x1": 0.4627379154929577,
        "y1": 0.8547712515180834
      },
      "text": "LOP-LOACH. The leech used by surgeons for drawing blood. North.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.030768225352112672,
        "y0": 0.8583317268965518,
        "x1": 0.3595024225352112,
        "y1": 0.8687728852277836
      },
      "text": "LOPLOLLY. A lazy fellow. West.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.031173070422535205,
        "y0": 0.8731788701724138,
        "x1": 0.2886561545915493,
        "y1": 0.8820973595803411
      },
      "text": "LOPPING. Lame. Dorset.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.031173070422535205,
        "y0": 0.8866641425517242,
        "x1": 0.37650591549295775,
        "y1": 0.8954521174805109
      },
      "text": "LOP-SIDED. One-sided. Var. dial.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.031173070422535205,
        "y0": 0.9000449701379309,
        "x1": 0.46193146411267594,
        "y1": 0.9220385416509467
      },
      "text": "LOP-START. The stoat. East. It is mentioned in Harrison's England, p. 230.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.03157791549295774,
        "y0": 0.9263345348455173,
        "x1": 0.261533154253521,
        "y1": 0.9359988114588016
      },
      "text": "LOPUSTER. A lobster.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.032387605633802816,
        "y0": 0.939303153648276,
        "x1": 0.39513526625352097,
        "y1": 0.9626436781609196
      },
      "text": "LOPWEBBE. A spider's web. (^.-5-.) II",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5493747605633802,
        "y0": 0.07584534718758626,
        "x1": 0.8481504225352112,
        "y1": 0.09564537057681263
      },
      "text": "As a lopwebbe filetli fome and gnattis. Taken and suffren gret files go.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48945769014084506,
        "y0": 0.10162463155724144,
        "x1": 0.9214273802816901,
        "y1": 0.12099121938636703
      },
      "text": "Occleve, MS. Soc. Jntiq. 134, f. 267. LOQUINTUE. Eloquent. Weber.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48945769014084506,
        "y0": 0.12388819764000006,
        "x1": 0.9202087966197185,
        "y1": 0.1480896094787589
      },
      "text": "LORD. (1) A title of honour given to monks and persons of superior rank. {A.-S.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4890528450704225,
        "y0": 0.15254944465517256,
        "x1": 0.9206184998309856,
        "y1": 0.2427059489975923
      },
      "text": "(2) Lord have mercy upon us was formerly the inscription on houses infected with the plague. Lord have mercy upon me, a disease thus mentioned in the Nomenclator, \"the IlUake passion, or a paine and wringing in the small guts, which the homelier sort of phisicians doe call, Lorde have mercy upon me.\"",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48743346478873234,
        "y0": 0.24562450891172427,
        "x1": 0.9206209289014087,
        "y1": 0.2805761920198959
      },
      "text": "LORDEYN. See Fever- Licrden. \" The lurgyfever, idleness,\" Craven Glossary, p. 304. I trow he was infecte certeyn",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.546136,
        "y0": 0.2851872598813794,
        "x1": 0.8440954943098592,
        "y1": 0.2926311551354049
      },
      "text": "With the faitour, or the fever lurdeyn.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7125273239436619,
        "y0": 0.2975574186924139,
        "x1": 0.9193991064788732,
        "y1": 0.3053555023647234
      },
      "text": "MS. Rawl. C . 86, xv. Cent.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4862189295774647,
        "y0": 0.3109711333793105,
        "x1": 0.919803951549296,
        "y1": 0.3470011234590933
      },
      "text": "LORD-FEST. Excessively lordly. (A.-S.) LORDINGS. Sirs ; masters. (A.~S.) It is often used bv later writers in contempt.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48581408450704217,
        "y0": 0.3511093491406897,
        "x1": 0.919808,
        "y1": 0.4952533516546242
      },
      "text": "LORD-OF-MISRULE. The person who presided over the Christmas revels, by no means an unimportant personage in the olden times. He began his rule on All-hallow eve and continued it till Candlemas day. See a hst of expences, dated in 1552, in Kempe's Loseley Manuscripts, pp. 44-54. For further information on the subject, see Brand, i. 272 ; Arch, xviii, 313-335 ; Hawkins' Engl. Dram. iii. 156; Strutt, ii. 200 ; Lilly's Sixe Court Comedies, 12mo. 1632, sig. F.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48459954929577465,
        "y0": 0.4999327373117242,
        "x1": 0.9165651909859148,
        "y1": 0.523008917295532
      },
      "text": "LORDS-AND-LADIES. See Bulls-and-Cows. LORDSHIP. Supreme power. (J.-S.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4850043943661972,
        "y0": 0.5274797281227587,
        "x1": 0.8509843380281689,
        "y1": 0.5362698243259689
      },
      "text": "LORD-SIZE. The judge at the assizes.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48459954929577465,
        "y0": 0.5406752510703449,
        "x1": 0.917370832676056,
        "y1": 0.5632261331541253
      },
      "text": "LORD'S-ROOM. The stage-box in a theatre was formerly so called. Jonson.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48459954929577465,
        "y0": 0.5668853485296552,
        "x1": 0.8056473579718307,
        "y1": 0.5776159886760595
      },
      "text": "LORDSWYK. A traitor. Eifson.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48378985915492956,
        "y0": 0.5813593649503448,
        "x1": 0.9161635846760561,
        "y1": 0.5911603630433397
      },
      "text": "LORE. (1) Knowledge ; doctrine ; advice. (J.-S.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48459954929577465,
        "y0": 0.5969376217779311,
        "x1": 0.8007746427042254,
        "y1": 0.6047476198311498
      },
      "text": "(2) Lost. Still in use in Somerset.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5627346478873239,
        "y0": 0.6083218217420691,
        "x1": 0.8457148745915494,
        "y1": 0.6159595290613651
      },
      "text": "The kyng seld. Take me thy tayle.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5619249577464788,
        "y0": 0.6209901747737931,
        "x1": 0.8432858041690141,
        "y1": 0.6402078411380956
      },
      "text": "For my hors I wolde not the fayle, A peny that thou lore.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6902608450704224,
        "y0": 0.6447155566234483,
        "x1": 0.9113046341408448,
        "y1": 0.6525876354922933
      },
      "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. v. 48, f. 61.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4825753239436619,
        "y0": 0.6553891751724138,
        "x1": 0.9153506557746476,
        "y1": 0.6787057140647399
      },
      "text": "LOREFADYR. A teacher. Loremastir, Dial. Great. Moral, p. 243.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5222501408450704,
        "y0": 0.6834644955710346,
        "x1": 0.7469351064788732,
        "y1": 0.6907158800320751
      },
      "text": "Of al men they do most evy].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48176563380281684,
        "y0": 0.6957067138468966,
        "x1": 0.9141385496338026,
        "y1": 0.7168757128139904
      },
      "text": "Here lorefadyr ys thedevyl. MS, Harl. 1701, f 24. LOREINE. A rein. See Launfal, 888.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5611152676056337,
        "y0": 0.7211290472951725,
        "x1": 0.8295259299154927,
        "y1": 0.7285089567837093
      },
      "text": "Hys loreine lemyd alle with pride,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5619249577464788,
        "y0": 0.7339979343296551,
        "x1": 0.8169708745915492,
        "y1": 0.740431876201774
      },
      "text": "Stede and armure alle was blake.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7437003943661971,
        "y0": 0.747839800808276,
        "x1": 0.9153514654647887,
        "y1": 0.7529872918655732
      },
      "text": "2lf5:. Har/. 22.52, f. 104.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48176563380281684,
        "y0": 0.7582233131034483,
        "x1": 0.9149466203943664,
        "y1": 0.8217170943357777
      },
      "text": "LOREL. A bad worthless fellow. {A.-N.) Lorels den, Holinshed, Chron. Ireland, p. 93. Cocke Lorel was formerly a generic title for a very great rascal. \" Lasy lorrels,\" Harman, 1567.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4813607887323943,
        "y0": 0.8258556009806897,
        "x1": 0.9129304919436618,
        "y1": 0.8488655809371701
      },
      "text": "LOREMAR. A bit-maker. Palsgrave. \"Lorimers or bit-makers,\" Harrison, p. 97.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4813607887323943,
        "y0": 0.8530809910344828,
        "x1": 0.5882398873239436,
        "y1": 0.862652052838112
      },
      "text": "LORENGE.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6125305915492957,
        "y0": 0.8555724367048275,
        "x1": 0.6554401205633804,
        "y1": 0.861720538768868
      },
      "text": "Iron.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6760912676056338,
        "y0": 0.8546743006896551,
        "x1": 0.7441052394366197,
        "y1": 0.8616350729104764
      },
      "text": "{A.-N.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48095594366197175,
        "y0": 0.8668099679310345,
        "x1": 0.8198177451267603,
        "y1": 0.8759911262148501
      },
      "text": "LORER. The laurel- tree. Chaucer.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5607104225352112,
        "y0": 0.8805451396551724,
        "x1": 0.7853961978591548,
        "y1": 0.8870708636121923
      },
      "text": "This Daphne into a lorer tre",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5615201126760563,
        "y0": 0.8917205392386206,
        "x1": 0.8299259168450703,
        "y1": 0.8994539571759531
      },
      "text": "Was tumid, whiche is ever grene.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6542296338028168,
        "y0": 0.9046034414510346,
        "x1": 0.9125240274929574,
        "y1": 0.9116089424622246
      },
      "text": "Gower, MS. Soc. Antiq. 134, f. 96.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5412778591549295,
        "y0": 0.917474400035862,
        "x1": 0.8461197196619717,
        "y1": 0.9367452337078515
      },
      "text": "And plaunted trees that were to preise, Of cidre, palmS; and of torere.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.57488,
        "y0": 0.9418974731034484,
        "x1": 0.9117110985915492,
        "y1": 0.9488582453242697
      },
      "text": "Cursor Mundi, MS. Coll. Trin. Cantab, f.52,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
  ],
